  "id": "Hounslow-PA_2026_0809",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Application for prior approval under Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA for proposed new dwellinghouses on detached building in commercial or mixed use by the upward extension of one additional storey to provide 10no. apartments. \n\n\n",
  "development_type": "Notifications",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal involves non-engineering operations such as the erection of gable roof extensions to the building. The provisions of Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA of the Town and County Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order (2015) (as amended) do not allow external material changes other than engineering operations reasonably necessary to construct the additional storeys. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the terms of Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA of the Town and County Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order (2015) (as amended). ",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal fails to ensure the transport impacts of the development are adequately addressed, due to the overprovision of car parking. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the terms of Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA, Paragraph AA.2 (a) of the Town and County Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order (2015) (as amended).",
    "Reason : 3 - In the absence of an assessment of daylight and sunlight impacts on neighbouring premises in particular, the proposal fails to demonstrate that it would not result in an unacceptable loss of light to the amenity of neighbouring properties, contrary to the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development)(England) Order 2015 (as amended), Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA, Paragraph AA.2 (g) of the Town and County Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order (2015) (as amended)."
  ],
